    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49422.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Well, we're hearing about it everywhere and it's, you know, it's real. I mean, it's painful and it's not a lot of disposable income for people in Ohio and you can be a home health care worker. You know, some a few weeks ago up in the northern part of the state, service workers in the southern part of the state. I think we need a tax cut right now for those workers. We got to immediately put some money in their pocket, whether it's the, you know, the child and family tax cut that we did last year that people got or earn income tax credit that would help working class people who are out working doing everything right or just a general tax cut for workers that we can advance so that they have money in their pocket. They don't have to wait until next year's tax returns. let's get that money in their pocket now and then we've got a you know yeah of course you know i mean i know everybody want to you know point the finger but we had we do have a war going on a significant war with an oil and gas producing country in russia uh... ukraine is the bread basket of europe so that it's affecting food costs with with what's going on uh... and now we and then the supply chain that you know a bunch democrats and republicans allow these jobs to leave america for China and other places. So now, you know, we're relying on China. They have a uptick in COVID. Now they have a zero tolerance policy for COVID. So they're shutting everything down. So that's affecting it. So tax cut in the short term and bring these jobs back in the short mid the long term so that we're making stuff here. We're less reliant on them. And we have more control of our own destiny in the United States and not relying on a communist country like China.",
