  {
    "episode_id": 49422,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49422.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, I don't think Vladimir Putin should end up with one inch of territory in Ukraine. I think we need to continue to arm the Ukrainians and allow them to push him out of their country. I think we need to get him airplanes if we can to protect the airspace. We're continuing to see these kind of war crimes. They need to protect their airspace. I'm a little more aggressive on this kind of thing. because it's an issue of freedom. And I don't think this kind of violence should be rewarded. This is not how we solve problems in the global community. This is a democratically elected country in Ukraine. And we need to be more forceful and get this equipment to them quicker and more of it. And I think that's important. And here we are in the middle of an election. You know, tens of thousands of Ukrainians here in Ohio who have family there and a guy like JD Vance says he doesn't care what's going on in Ukraine. When people are getting slaughtered and more crimes, I think it speaks a little bit to his lack of understanding of, you know, and in humanity. I mean, I'm not saying we need to send troops over there, but my goodness gracious, we are the United States. I can't let it blad in your Putin. auto-crat like him roll into another country to start killing people this doesn't work that way and united states need to be strong we need to be aggressive and the uh... Ukrainians are showing amazing resolve and strength and we need to be there to support them and in the Ukrainian americans and end up in the peep in the people in polander worried people with the way near worried and a lot of these others countries there because well who's next if we like a lot of their people do this and give them You know, put up the flag of appeasement like JB Vance wants to do. They're going to storm right through Europe and we can't have that again. We bet that that happened many, many years ago in the United States and the American people stepped up to make sure that doesn't happen. We need to do that again, again, not sending troops, but make sure we we're supplying Ukraine with what they need.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Vladimir Putin should not gain any territory in Ukraine.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The United States should continue arming Ukraine.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Ukraine needs fighter aircraft to defend its airspace.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "War crimes are currently being committed by Russian forces.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Supporting Ukraine is an issue of freedom.",
        "confidence": 0.91
